From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:06:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] docs(r64): Fable-check gates - corrected counts, paired
 cites, generators, served pairing

All six docs gates from CHECK-R64-FABLE.md (PASS-GATED). No GPU touched; two
other makers own it. The only source change is a comment.

(1) COUNTS. Two numbers were line counts wearing a case count's clothes. The
planted RED is 52/85 = 33 FAIL cases, not 35 (the extra two were the backend
and run summary lines); the targeted gate is 152 cases (q5_K 85 + q6_K 67),
not 160 (the extra eight were wrapped / not-supported lines). Neither moves a
verdict, but a grep count presented as a receipt count is exactly what this
report tells others not to trust. Strengthened while correcting: every one of
the 33 failed cases is at n=5..8 and none below, so the RED discriminates at
case granularity and not just in aggregate.

(2) CITES. Report 3b and 3d named the paired files while printing the
UNPAIRED medians from 12-table-all.txt. Replaced with the paired values and
their rounds-won. The k=17408 route arm is 1.008/1.002/1.063/0.983 (4/6, 4/6,
5/6, 2/6) and q6_K now carries a three-shape paired table. Same conclusions,
right tables.

(3) The struct comment at ggml-vulkan.cpp:1471 still said n=2..8. Now n=5..8,
matching the code, the receipt string and the registry.

(4) GENERATORS COMMITTED. r64-typemix.py and r64-paired.py replace the inline
one-offs, and both reproduce their tables exactly (13-paired-down-head.txt now
also carries n=1..4, which the one-off truncated; every n=5..8 value is
unchanged). New 11-shapes.txt is the tensor listing behind the two shape
claims the report makes by name, each printed with its evidence under it:
"no Q5_K at m=248320" -> 0 tensors, CLAIM A HOLDS; and the per-type (k,m)
census behind "90.5% of Q5_K bytes at k<=8192".

(5) Report section 0 over-attributed the 128 us/col to a gated-off hoist. Its
own section 5 shows the f32 shader WITH that hoist on loses 30-180% at n=4..8,
so the cost is the f32 dequant route AS SUCH; the lever is to leave that route,
not repair it. Sentence withdrawn.

(6) New section 6b carries HQ's served pairing (chain149), flagged throughout
as HQ's evidence and not the maker's. PPL at batch 8 - the batch where the
route is actually exercised, a default-batch cell runs n=512 through mul_mm and
would have been inert - reads 5.9918 legacy vs 5.9932 route against +/-0.143,
identical inside one stderr; served df2 tie, plain arm noise, rolled40 37/37.
With the expected-effect arithmetic beside it: ~+0.7% at n=5, ceiling ~+1.8%,
0% at n=4 because the route is inert there. So a tie IS the prediction, and a
gain above ~2% would mean the attribution is wrong rather than the lever
better. This lane buys correctness of the route table, not the 15-20 t/s
target.

Also records that the "R48b ship rule" is the brief's rule, not R48b's own
(R48b was bit-identical by construction and needed none), and files HQ's
60-build-ppl-server.txt - HQ's build log for the cells above, not the maker's.

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-252 R64 q5_K MMVQ route, Opus 5 MEDIUM kernel-maker)
Measured-effect: op-level perf-mode only (rows in receipts); served t/s UNMEASURED by the maker - the section 6b numbers are HQ's chain149 cells
Lane: lane-252
Cherry-picked-from: 7a771f37b (SOURCE PATHS ONLY, ArifiLabs lane-254 R66 integration)
Recut-onto: 1b6185951 (ArifiLabs lane-254 R66c, from 818c70c26)
Conflict-resolved: S4 split (f172be756): auto_split - our hunks re-homed into ggml-vulkan-types.h; wrap/same-point regions merged in place (fixS4_648.py)
